               LogOff! V2.0 By Jeepster (AKA Thomas Newsom)
              ----------------------------------------------

If you've got this far you've already unpacked this :) Hopefully you've
done it into Pfiles:  or Doors:  If not, move the directory into one of
those directories.  Then we'll begin the full installation :)

Information 
------------

Logoff!.rexx v2.0 is an update from V1.0.  

V1.0 was a simple 'all in one' program.  Now you have the option off
showing you're own ANSI screen.  LogOff!  also has a new 'return to BBS'
option as well.

Included is an Ansi screen created by Smidge (Sharron Kingdon).

What is it?
------------

LogOff!.rexx is a program that users see at log off. It allows them to have
one of 4 options. Leave feedback, Check for waiting mail, Return to the BBS
or Log off fully.

New to v2.0
------------

v2.0 now allows the sysop to show there own Ansi/MCI created screens. This
file can be specified in the main code of the program. This is shown in the
porgram code itself. Also new in v2.0 is the user option to return to the
main proper.

How do I install this thing?
----------------------------

Installation is easy ;) There are several places in BBSMENU that you should
enter it. I strongly suggest you alter every option as specified.

In BBSMENU under '3; main prompt alter the 'Off' option so it shows '2Off'
then at the end of that particular menu add this

Off		|	#0pfiles:logoff/logoff!.rexx}
			|
			Control-q

Do the same for all instances of 'Off' in BBSMENU. It should appear in menu
numbers

 3; Main prompt
 4; ud/base
 6; News/GFiles/PFiles
14; Bbslist

Done that? Good :)

What can I alter?
-----------------

There are two variables in the main code that you can alter, these are
shown in the code so you'll find them easy enough. The variable 'ansi' can
be 1 or 0. 0 means use the built in screen. 1 means use the ansi/mci screen
specified in 'path'.

The other variable 'path' specifies the file AND full path of the ansi/mci
screen you want to use.

If you create your own ansi/mci screens remember to jave the following on
that screen somewhere.

F Feedback
C Check for mail
L Log off
R Return to BBS

How you show those commands is entirely upto you. But make sure you use
those leading letters (F,C,L,R) as thats what the program checks for.

Anything else?
--------------

Nope :) If you've done everything correctly then you should be fine :)

